{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.06,
   "end": 6.2,
   "text": "Same thousand dollars, same S and P five hundred. One friend ends with ten times as much. Guess what the other two did."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 6.34,
   "end": 12.7,
   "text": "They buy in at the start of two thousand six. The two thousand eight crash shrinks each one to seven seventy. One new phone."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 12.88,
   "end": 16.02,
   "text": "Jay panics, sells, and hides the cash in a shoebox."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 16.18,
   "end": 18.64,
   "text": "Maya sells too, then buys back a year later."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 18.86,
   "end": 21.12,
   "text": "Sam holds and lets his dividends reinvest."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 21.26,
   "end": 26.0,
   "text": "By twenty thirteen, Sam's money is worth over two phones. Jay's shoebox? Still one."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 26.14,
   "end": 29.4,
   "text": "By twenty nineteen, over four phones. Jay? Still one."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 29.54,
   "end": 34.82,
   "text": "End of twenty twenty-five, Sam's at over ten phones, about eight thousand dollars. Jay? Still one."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 34.98,
   "end": 37.22,
   "text": "And Maya? Same as Sam, except one year."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 37.38,
   "end": 40.16,
   "text": "About eight phones. That one missed year cost her two."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 40.36,
   "end": 43.46,
   "text": "So if your money crashed tomorrow, would you sell, wait or hold?"
  }
